{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Pacific Mall is an Asian shopping centre in Markham, Ontario, Canada.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located on the northeast side of Steeles Avenue and Kennedy Road, right across the municipal border from the city of Toronto, on the site formerly occupied by Cullen Country Barns.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The two entrance roads of the mall are Redlea Avenue and Clayton Drive.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Pacific Mall is surrounded by an existing shopping plaza, including the Market Village, and together they encompass over 500 stores and are served by both indoor and outdoor parking areas with over 1,500 parking spaces combined.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It has two floors and an underground level that leads to an underground parking lot.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Designed by Wallman Clewes Bergman Architects, their first proposal was modified by the aesthetic expectations of Markham Town Council (now City Council).","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Pacific Mall first opened its doors for business in 1997.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Its Cantonese name, "太古廣場" (Tai Gu Gwong Cheung), is derived from Pacific Place in Hong Kong.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" The mall has a total of 270000 sqft of retail space.","title":"Pacific Mall"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Splendid China Mall (Traditional Chinese: 錦繡中華; Simplified Chinese: 锦绣中华) (formerly known as Splendid China Tower) is a 90000 sqft Chinese-themed ethnic shopping centre located at the southeast corner of Redlea Avenue and Steeles Avenue in the Scarborough district of Toronto, Ontario, Canada.","title":"Splendid China Mall"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located adjacent to Milliken GO Station and across from the Pacific Mall along with the Market Village.","title":"Splendid China Mall"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The structure was formerly occupied by Canadian Tire.","title":"Splendid China Mall"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Splendid China was a theme park in Four Corners, Florida near Disney World and Orlando.","title":"Splendid China (Florida)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It opened in 1993, and closed on December 31, 2003.","title":"Splendid China (Florida)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was a sister park to Splendid China in Shenzhen, China which is still open and receives many visitors.","title":"Splendid China (Florida)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Florida Splendid China cost $100 million to build.","title":"Splendid China (Florida)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"New South China Mall () in Dongguan, China is the largest shopping mall in the world when measured in terms of gross leasable area, and second in terms of total area to The Dubai Mall (which has extensive non-shopping space including a zoo, a hotel complex and a theme park).","title":"South China Mall"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" South China Mall opened in 2005 and for more than 10 years it was mostly vacant as few merchants ever signed up, leading it to be dubbed a dead mall.","title":"South China Mall"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 2015 a CNN story reported that the mall had begun to attract tenants after extensive renovations and remodeling, though large portions remained vacant.","title":"South China Mall"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Remington Centre (滙通廣場) is an 800,000 sqft Chinese-themed mall to be built at the corner of Kennedy Road and Steeles Avenue in Markham, Ontario, Canada, on the site of the present Market Village mall.","title":"Remington Centre"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It will be connected to Pacific Mall by an indoor walkway.","title":"Remington Centre"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Market Village is scheduled for demolition and construction of the new mall was to have begun in the third quarter of 2013, but as of early 2017, Market Village remains in operation with no signs of closure, but some long term tenants have left including McDonald's in late 2015.","title":"Remington Centre"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" As of March 2017, certain stores have started selling off all inventory with sales staff mentioning the reason as store closing due to demolition work slated to begin September 2017.","title":"Remington Centre"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Yitian Holiday Plaza () is a shopping mall in Nanshan, Shenzhen, China.","title":"Yitian Holiday Plaza"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is located within the Overseas Chinese Town (OCT) area of Shenzhen, and a walking distance from a number of theme parks such as Window of the World and Splendid China.","title":"Yitian Holiday Plaza"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The mall features, amongst others, a Westin Hotel, an ice rink and the first Apple retail store in Shenzhen.","title":"Yitian Holiday Plaza"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Steeles Avenue
